## 8. Full call lifecycle — end-to-end

### 8.1 Outgoing (caller side)

```
1. User taps ☎️ (voice) or 📹 (video)
        ↓
2. POST /api/calls/create  { callee_id, call_type }
        → { call_id }
        ↓
3. getUserMedia({ audio: true, video: mode === 'video' })
        ↓
4. new RTCPeerConnection (STUN servers)
        ↓
5. pc.createOffer() → pc.setLocalDescription(offer)
        ↓
6. POST /api/calls/signal  { call_id, to_user_id, type: "offer", payload: offer }
        ↓
7. Start polling every 900ms:
   GET /api/calls/poll?call_id=&after=
        ↓
8. Receives "accept" → setCallPhase("connecting")
        ↓
9. Receives "answer" → pc.setRemoteDescription(answer)
        ↓
10. Receives "ice" candidates → pc.addIceCandidate
        ↓
11. pc.connectionState === "connected" → setCallPhase("active"), start timer
```

### 8.2 Incoming (callee side)

```
1. Polling every 1200ms:
   GET /api/calls/incoming
        → { call: { id, caller_id, call_type, status: "ringing" } }
        ↓
2. Show incoming UI + play ringtone
        ↓
3. User taps "Accept":
        ↓
   POST /api/calls/signal  { call_id, to_user_id, type: "accept", payload: { ok: true } }
        ↓
   getUserMedia({ audio: true, video: mode === 'video' })
        ↓
   new RTCPeerConnection
        ↓
   Start polling every 900ms:
   GET /api/calls/poll?call_id=&after=
        ↓
   Receives "offer" → pc.setRemoteDescription(offer) → pc.createAnswer()
        ↓
   pc.setLocalDescription(answer)
        ↓
   POST /api/calls/signal  { call_id, to_user_id, type: "answer", payload: answer }
        ↓
   Receives "ice" candidates → pc.addIceCandidate
        ↓
   pc.connectionState === "connected" → setCallPhase("active"), start timer
```

### 8.3 Ending a call (either side)

```
User taps hangup:
        ↓
POST /api/calls/signal  { call_id, to_user_id, type: "hangup", payload: { ok: true } }
        ↓
Local cleanup:
  - stopRingtone()
  - stopCallTimer()
  - stopPollingCallEvents()
  - close RTCPeerConnection
  - stop all local media tracks
  - logMissedOnce() if outgoing & never connected
        ↓
Remote side receives "hangup" on next poll → endCall(true)
```

### 8.4 Declining a call (callee side)

```
User taps Decline:
        ↓
POST /api/calls/signal  { call_id, to_user_id, type: "decline", payload: { reason: "declined" } }
        ↓
Caller receives "decline" → logMissedOnce() → shows "Missed voice/video call" message
```

### 8.5 Missed-call log

If a call ends without ever connecting, `logMissedOnce()` sends a **chat message** via `POST /api/messages/send`:

```tsx
const logMissedOnce = async (callId: string, args: { mode: "voice" | "video"; direction: "incoming" | "outgoing" }) => {
  if (!callId) return;
  if (missedLoggedRef.current.has(callId)) return;
  missedLoggedRef.current.add(callId);
  if (missedLoggedRef.current.size > 200) missedLoggedRef.current = new Set();
  await sendCallLog({ kind: "missed", mode: args.mode, direction: args.direction });
};

const sendCallLog = async (args: { kind: "missed" | "ended"; mode: "voice" | "video"; direction: "incoming" | "outgoing" }) => {
  const icon = args.mode === "video" ? "🎥" : "📞";
  const title = args.kind === "missed" ? `Missed ${args.mode} call` : `${args.mode === "video" ? "Video" : "Voice"} call`;
  const text = `${icon} ${title}`;

  try {
    await send({
      recipient_id: (recipient as any)?.id,
      text_content: text,
    });
  } catch {}
};
```

This produces the message `"📞 Missed voice call"` or `"🎥 Missed video call"` in the conversation — which renders through `CallMessage` with a "Call back" button.

